  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Hari Ram Shukla vs State Of U.P.And Another on 22 August, 2019 Author: Sudhir Agarwal Bench: Sudhir Agarwal High Court Of Judicature At Allahabad ?Court No. - 34 Case :- Criminal Revision No. - 1662 of 1992 Revisionist :- Hari Ram Shukla Opposite Party :- State Of U.P.And Another Counsel for Revisionist :- V.B. Rao Counsel for Opposite Party :- A.G.A. Hon'ble Sudhir Agarwal,J. 1. Heard Sri V. B. Rao, learned counsel for revisionist and learned A.G.A. for State. 2. This criminal revision under Section 397/401 Cr.P.C., has been filed aggrieved by the judgments and orders dated 14.07.1992 and 21.11.1992.",
    "facts": "",
    "arguments": "1 preferred present revision. 3. Learned counsel for revisionist contended that revisionist has been convicted for want of license though it could not be shown that he was selling the milk, but it is evident from record that Revisionist possessed 25 litres of Milk in a container and no valid explanation could be offered by Revisionist for the same.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "1 preferred present revision. 3. Learned counsel for revisionist contended that revisionist has been convicted for want of license though it could not be shown that he was selling the milk, but it is evident from record that Revisionist possessed 25 litres of Milk in a container and no valid explanation could be offered by Revisionist for the same.",
